Fix TypeError from call_user_func() on a "service:method" access callback

The content_translation access callback is defined as the string
"content_translation.manager:access" (Drupal's service:method callable
notation). Plain call_user_func() cannot resolve that notation, so it throws
"TypeError: call_user_func(): Argument #1 ($callback) must be a valid callback,
function 'content_translation.manager:access' not found or invalid function
name" on Drupal 11.4.1.

Resolve the definition through the callable_resolver service so the real access
callback actually runs, and degrade to the per-entity permission check if the
definition is genuinely unresolvable.

Issue: https://www.drupal.org/project/auto_node_translate/issues/3609236

--- a/src/Access/AutoNodeTranslateAccessCheck.php
+++ b/src/Access/AutoNodeTranslateAccessCheck.php
@@ -54,7 +54,17 @@
       $definition = $this->entityTypeManager->getDefinition($entity_type_id);
       $translation = $definition->get('translation');
       $access_callback = $translation['content_translation']['access_callback'];
-      $access = call_user_func($access_callback, $entity);
+      // The access callback is defined as a "service:method" string, which
+      // call_user_func() cannot resolve on its own. Resolve it through the
+      // callable resolver so the real access check runs; fall through to the
+      // permission check below if the definition is not resolvable.
+      try {
+        $callable = \Drupal::service('callable_resolver')->getCallableFromDefinition($access_callback);
+        $access = call_user_func($callable, $entity);
+      }
+      catch (\InvalidArgumentException $e) {
+        $access = AccessResult::neutral();
+      }
       if ($access->isAllowed()) {
         return $access;
       }
